<article class="env-lemma" id="0DEP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DEP">Lemma <span data-tag="0DEP">21.18.7</span>.</a> Let $f : (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \mathcal{O}) \to (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}'), \mathcal{O}')$ be a morphism of ringed topoi. If $\mathcal{C}$ has enough points, then the pullback of a K-flat complex of $\mathcal{O}'$-modules is a K-flat complex of $\mathcal{O}$-modules. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0DEN" data-tag="0DEN">21.18.6</a>, Modules on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/05V5" data-tag="05V5">18.36.4</a>, and More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/06Y1" data-tag="06Y1">15.60.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>